---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import InstallCommand from "@/components/InstallCommand.astro";
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Layout title="Installation" description="Install loseta in a native CSS project.">
  <div class="docs-content">
    <p class="docs-eyebrow">Getting started</p>
    <h1>Installation</h1>
    <p class="docs-lead">
      loseta copies CSS files into your project. You need Node 20+ and a CSS entrypoint.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Initialize</h2>
    <p>The CLI detects a CSS entrypoint and creates the foundation files.</p>
    <InstallCommand command="loseta init" />
    <p>
      If you prefer to answer every question explicitly, omit <code>--yes</code>. The CLI asks for
      the CSS directory, the theme and the entrypoint.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Add components</h2>
    <p>Components install their structural CSS, the Nova theme file and any primitive dependency.</p>
    <InstallCommand command="loseta add button card field dialog" />
    <p>To install every stable component:</p>
    <InstallCommand command="loseta add all" />

    <h2>3. Import the generated entrypoint</h2>
    <p>
      <code>init</code> creates <code>loseta/index.css</code> and can add a single import to your
      CSS entrypoint. If you skipped that step, add it manually:
    </p>
    <CodeBlock lang="css" code={`@import "./styles/loseta/index.css";`} />

    <h2>Project files</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="text"
      code={`loseta.json                 # cssDir, entrypoint and theme
.loseta/manifest.json       # installed items and file hashes
src/styles/loseta/
  tokens.css                 # design tokens
  reset.css                  # minimal reset
  base.css                   # element defaults
  utilities.css              # sr-only
  index.css                  # generated @layer order + imports
  primitives/                # shared popover/dialog shells
  components/                # structural CSS per component
  themes/nova/               # visual CSS per component`}
    />

    <h2>Commands</h2>
    <p>The CLI works with pnpm and npm. The examples use pnpm.</p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="bash"
      code={`pnpm dlx loseta init               # set up the project
pnpm dlx loseta add button card    # add components
pnpm dlx loseta add all            # add every stable component
pnpm dlx loseta list               # list components
pnpm dlx loseta list --all         # include primitives and foundation
pnpm dlx loseta add button --html  # print the example markup`}
    />

    <h2>Coexistence</h2>
    <p>
      loseta is a native CSS design system. It uses unprefixed classes such as
      <code>.btn</code> and unprefixed tokens such as <code>--background</code>. If your project
      already uses shadcn/ui or Tailwind, choose one token contract instead of loading both.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout">
      <strong>No build step required.</strong> The CSS uses native nesting, <code>@layer</code>,
      <code>:has()</code>, <code>color-mix()</code>, <code>@starting-style</code> and <code>field-sizing</code>.
      Target Chrome/Edge 125+, Safari 26+ and Firefox 147+ for full fidelity.
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
